      "Standard Temperature & Pressure (STP vs NTP): Standard conditions: $T = 273.15\\text{ K}$ ($0^\\circ\\text{C}$), $P = 1\\text{ atm} = 101.325\\text{ kPa}$; Standard molar volume of ideal gas at STP equals $22.414\\text{ L/mol} = 22.414\\text{ m}^3/\\text{kmol}$.",
      "Gas Mixtures (Dalton's & Amagat's Laws): Dalton's law of partial pressures: $p_i = y_i P_{total}$ where $y_i$ is gas-phase mole fraction; Amagat's law of partial volumes: $v_i = y_i V_{total}$; For ideal gas mixtures, volume percent equals mole percent.",
