      "Enzyme Inhibition Typology: Competitive inhibition (inhibitor competes with substrate for active site; increases apparent constant, maximum velocity unchanged; overcome by excess substrate); Non-competitive inhibition (inhibitor binds allosteric site; reduces maximum velocity, constant unchanged).",
      "Glycolysis (Embden-Meyerhof-Parnas Pathway): Cytoplasmic anaerobic catabolism of 1 glucose (6C) into 2 pyruvate (3C) molecules; Net energy yield: 2 ATP (via substrate-level phosphorylation) + 2 NADH; Rate-limiting committed step catalyzed by Phosphofructokinase (PFK).",
